cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Renascore: An open catalogue of digital editions of Renaissance-era written documents"
message: "If you use this catalogue in your research, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Godbarge
    given-names: Clément
    affiliation: "University of St Andrews"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pantagrueliste/renascore"
url: "https://renascore.github.io"
abstract: >-
  Renascore is an open catalogue of projects that have produced digital
  editions of Renaissance-era written documents (manuscripts, printed works,
  correspondence) from roughly 1450 to 1700. Each entry records the project
  title, URL, language, encoding format, status, and provenance.
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - renaissance
  - digital editions
  - catalogue
  - TEI
license: CC0-1.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-07
